  "goodToKnow": "Der Fabrikant is a manufacturer or factory owner, a slightly old-fashioned word evoking 19th-century industrialists, whose Fabrikantenvillen still stand in many towns. Today, companies are called Hersteller and owners Unternehmer. Gerhart Hauptmann's play Die Weber (1892) shows weavers rising against a Fabrikant. It's a weak noun: den Fabrikanten. Plural: die Fabrikanten."
